### Step 5: Get onboarding data for authenticated user (using access token)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/onboarding/user/data
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Step 6: Update onboarding data for authenticated user
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/onboarding/user/update
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "pregnancy_status": "pregnant",
  "last_period": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "cycle_length": 28,
  "period_length": 5,
  "pregnancy_week": 13,
  "pregnancy_progress": "first_trimester",
  "health_goals": "{\"track_period\": true, \"cycle_insights\": true, \"pregnancy_tracking\": true, \"nutrition_tips\": true}",
  "notifications": true
}

### Step 7: Test direct registration with onboarding data (alternative flow)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "direct-onboarding@example.com",
  "phone": "+1234567897",
  "onboardingData": {
    "pregnancy_status": "tracking",
    "last_period": "2024-10-01T00:00:00.000Z",
    "cycle_length": 30,
    "period_length": 6,
    "health_goals": "{\"track_period\": true, \"cycle_insights\": true}",
    "notifications": true
  }
}

### Verify email for direct registration
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "direct-onboarding@example.com",
  "verify_code": "123456"
}

### Login for direct registration user
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "direct-onboarding@example.com"
}

